{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>The burden of Tyre.</b> Tyre is upon the sea, and Nebuchadnezzar captured it." "<b>For it is devastated, every house.</b> In Tyre, that no merchant will come." "<b>From the land of Kittim.</b> Even from the land of Kittim, which is far away, this devastation was made known to them. And he mentioned Kittim because of the ships; the witness: \"and ships from the coast of Kittim\" (Numbers 24:24)."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:54:44.193131810Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}